1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Everyone photographs the Terracotta Army — almost no one sees what's hidden here.
{\fs13}I'm your China Travel Expert

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,000
Dug up in 1974 by farmers sinking a well: about 8,000 soldiers near Xi'an.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,300
Insider truth — each one was once painted in bright reds, greens and purples.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,800
Exposed to the dry air, that colour curls in 15 seconds and flakes off in minutes.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:17,000
And the real prize — Qin Shi Huang's tomb mound — has never been opened.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,300
Ancient texts say rivers of mercury run inside. Dig it, or leave it sealed?
